1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:04,560
 Sales is 20% the words you say and 80% your confidence and conviction.

2
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:08,160
 People don't buy because they understand you, they buy because they feel understood.

3
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:12,580
 Young people buy the dream, older people buy security, business owners buy time, alphas

4
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:16,620
 need to feel like it was their idea, betas need a clear direct game plan and empowerment.

5
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:20,360
 Sales is 80-20, they talk 80%, you talk 20%.

6
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:23,020
 Whoever asks the questions controls the conversation.

7
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:25,320
 Don't sell the steak, sell the sizzle of it.

8
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,320
 Stop yapping, don't over educate, sales is a dance.

9
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:30,360
 Sometimes you push, sometimes you pull back.

10
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:33,080
 People buy with emotion but justify with logic.

11
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:36,000
 Sell the gap between where they're at versus where they want to be.

12
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:38,480
 Don't pitch until you fully understand their problem.

13
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:39,860
 Make them sell themselves.

14
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:43,660
 Push past smoke screens, the first objection is almost never the real objection.

15
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:47,400
 Objections aren't bad, they're proof that someone's processing a buying decision.

16
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:49,400
 Common ground is where the deal is found.

17
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:52,620
 Identity selling is making the client live up to the person that they want to become.

18
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:54,480
 After you say price, shut up.

19
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:57,180
 Urgency isn't one spot left, it's the cost of inaction.

20
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:58,280
 Slow down.

